[00:00.00]Wilbur and Orville Wright are the American inventors who made a small engine-powered flying machine.
[00:09.89]They proved that flight without the aid of gas-filled balloons was possible.
[00:17.72]Wilbur Wright was born in 1867 near Melville, Indiana.
[00:25.22]His brother Orville was born four years later in Dayton, Ohio.
[00:32.06]As they grew up, the Wright brothers experimented with mechanical things.
